Certainly! Below is a concise 4-step execution playbook for an automated agent or Chrome CDP script to follow:

### 4-Step Execution Playbook

#### Step 1: Switch to List View
```javascript
// Assuming the list view is initially hidden or not in focus
document.querySelector('.list-view-toggle').click();
```

#### Step 2: Select All Items (up to 200/page)
```javascript
// Click the select-all checkbox in the table header
document.querySelector('.select-all-checkbox').click();

// Wait for the 'Selected Items: X/200' button to appear
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1000)); // Adjust timeout if necessary

// Verify the selection
const selectedItemsCount = document.querySelector('.selected-items-count').innerText;
console.log(`Selected Items: ${selectedItemsCount}`);
```

#### Step 3: Open the Batch Modal
```javascript
// Click the batch action button to open the modal
document.querySelector('.batch-action-button').click();

// Wait for the batch modal to load
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1000)); // Adjust timeout if necessary
```

#### Step 4: Either 'Add To My Products' or 'Export' Thousands of Items at Once
```javascript
// Check if the 'Add To My Products' button is available
const addToListButton = document.querySelector('.add-to-my-products');
if (addToListButton) {
    addToListButton.click();
} else {
    // If not available, check for the 'Export' button
    const exportButton = document.querySelector('.export-button');
    if (exportButton) {
        exportButton.click();
    } else {
        console.error('Neither "Add To My Products" nor "Export" button found.');
    }
}
```

### Notes:
- Ensure that the selectors (`class` or `id` attributes) used in the script match the actual UI elements on the page.
- Adjust the `setTimeout` intervals if the UI elements take longer to load or if the script needs to wait for additional events.
- Consider adding error handling to manage cases where elements might not be present or the script encounters unexpected behavior.
